Debian/Ubuntu packaging for the Kalman module
============================================

The native module and compiler metadata belong to qore-kalman-module.
HTML documentation and upstream example tests belong to the optional doc
package. Debhelper creates matching debug symbols. Eigen headers are compiled
into the module; its complete distribution copyright/license notices are
included as Eigen-copyright. No Eigen headers or shared library are bundled.

Build prerequisites and scope
-----------------------------

Use an isolated native environment with the packaged Qore runtime and
libqore-dev, then install debian/control's Build-Depends. The qualification
target is Ubuntu 26.04 amd64 with Qore 3.0 development packages. Other targets
need matching SDKs and native tests. Cross builds are rejected because Qore
tools execute during compilation. Use distribution Eigen >= 3.3.

The build uses distribution compiler and hardening flags. Native Qore modules
resolve Qore symbols at load time without linking libqore. debian/rules derives
a minimum runtime and libqore SONAME package dependency from the installed SDK;
dh_shlibdeps supplies other shared-library dependencies. The runtime is not
Multi-Arch: same. No AOT user modules are shipped; ordinary dh_strip applies.

Source and binary builds
------------------------

Use a fresh version for each changed upload. This snapshot follows 1.1.0.
From a clean committed checkout:

    version=1.1.0+git20260928.1
    mkdir -p ../kalman-package-work
    git archive --format=tar --prefix="qore-kalman-module-$version/" \
        HEAD -- . ':!debian' | xz > \
        "../kalman-package-work/qore-kalman-module_$version.orig.tar.xz"
    tar -xf "../kalman-package-work/qore-kalman-module_$version.orig.tar.xz" \
        -C ../kalman-package-work
    cp -a debian "../kalman-package-work/qore-kalman-module-$version/"
    cd "../kalman-package-work/qore-kalman-module-$version"
    dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc

Extract the .dsc into a fresh directory, then run dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc
unprivileged with networking disabled. -B builds native/debug packages; -A
builds documentation. nodoc in DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS suppresses HTML generation,
and the nodoc build profile omits the doc package. Do not use nocheck for full
qualification; repeated/profile builds may use it. noopt follows dpkg flags.

Qualification and publication
-----------------------------

Run all four upstream suites: matrix operations and invalid dimensions,
linear/extended filters, tracking factories and batch behavior. Installed
tests copy only the scripts into a temporary directory, without source module
paths. A fresh qcc executable tests matrix inversion, named arguments and a
tracking filter update. No external service or optional Qore module is needed.

Check Lintian, debug symbols and hardening, runtime installation without SDK
or Eigen headers, documentation/debug coinstallation, dpkg -V, purge/reinstall,
and byte reproducibility across different build paths and job counts. Retain
source/package hashes, dependency inventories and logs. Testing-PPA publication
is separate from approval for a final general release.
